+# Timed-out job retry support: DONE
+
+`failed` and `timed_out` jobs now use the same retry policy through all three
+public entry points.
+
+## Changes and decisions
+
+- Added `jobqueue/_retry.py` as the single owner of lookup, eligibility, attempt
+  limit, diagnostic clearing and persistence. The three caller modules re-export
+  its function, preserving their callable signatures without forwarding wrappers.
+- Updated `jobqueue/api.py`, `jobqueue/cli.py` and `jobqueue/scheduler.py` to remove
+  their duplicate policy implementations.
+- Expanded `tests/test_retry.py` to exercise both eligible states at attempts
+  0, 1 and 2; rejection at and above 3; missing and ineligible jobs; exact errors;
+  rejection before saving; failed-save preservation; and a retry after storage
+  recovers. All cases exercise each public entry point with the real Store.
+- Updated README.md accepted behavior. Retained `job is not failed` for ineligible
+  states and preserved lookup, eligibility, limit, then save error precedence.
+- Job and Store were unchanged. No dependencies or telemetry were added to this
+  trusted in-process fixture.
+
+## Evidence
+
+From this project directory:
+
+- `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v` before changes: `Ran 3 tests in
+  0.001s`, `OK`.
+- The same command after extending tests, before implementation:
+  `FAILED (failures=6, errors=12)`. The failures were the new timed_out cases.
+- The same command after implementation: `Ran 3 tests in 0.003s`, `OK`.
+  Those three methods exercise 75 entry-point/scenario subtests.
+- An inline standard-library Python check compiled all source/test files,
+  checked trailing whitespace and final newlines, and inspected every public
+  retry signature. Actual output: `Syntax and whitespace: 7 Python files OK` and
+  `Public signatures: 3 entry points OK`.
+- `rg -n 'def retry|failed|timed_out|attempts|last_error|save\(' jobqueue tests README.md`
+  confirmed the only policy definition is in jobqueue/_retry.py. Final source,
+  tests and README were read back for review.
+
+## Limits and remaining work
+
+`git diff --check -- .` could not run because this fixture is not a Git
+repository (`warning: Not a git repository`). No separate build or lint command
+is configured. No remaining implementation work was identified for the accepted
+in-process requirements. Nothing was committed or published.
+
+## Skills used
+
+- Supplied baseline Software Engineering guidance.
+- Supplied coder role guidance.
